A||||5||Voyd||ecm trouble codes question||||5
Z||000000||Voyd||11-05-1999||12:24 PM||||hey, id like to know what happens to the codes stored in the computer? do they permanatly stay there if there has been an occurance of the code, or do they erase themselves after a certain amount of time without the problem arising?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||ka4nkf||11-05-1999||01:01 PM||||The codes stay in the computer. the best way to erase them is to disconect the battery for about 30 seconds. This will erase them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Voyd||11-05-1999||07:01 PM||||so if the ecm has never been reset, there is no way of knowing which code is current, and which code is very old (and already fixed)?||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-05-1999||08:26 PM||||there is no prioritizing of codes. they are just there or not. reset the ECM and if you have any real ones they will return.<P>you can reset the ECM on some Fieros by disconnecting the single orange wire in the harness by the battery. You won't loose the radio settings this way. If you can't find or don't have the orange disconnect then the only other methode is disconect the battery.||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||11-05-1999||11:09 PM||||Most GM ECM's are set to clear all codes after 50 starts without an the error conditions reoccuring.<P>Have too look, but I assume the Fiero code is set to that too.||||reg||1
Z||000005||dogtired||11-06-1999||03:59 AM||||While on the subject of ECM if anyone needs  a FREE ECM Code booklet and key go to the General Fiero Chat section and See Free Code Book and Key from Autozone or E-Mail me directly||||reg||10
